{{- define "wake_hypothesis_exhausted" -}}
Multiple coders failed on same task. Re-evaluate and act NOW:

1. Read task history — understand what was tried and why it failed
2. Determine if:
   - Task is impossible as specified → supersede with revised tasks:
     a. Re-read the task via {{binaryName}} get <task-id> --json to confirm it is still in a supersedable state (BLOCKED/REJECTED/READY).
        If status changed (e.g., task was claimed), skip supersede — the task is being actively worked.
     b. Write a tasks JSON file as a bare array — NOT a wrapper object:
        [{
          "id": "<new-task-id>",
          "desc": "<short task description>",
          "spec": "<spec path>",
          "done": "<falsifiable completion condition>",
          "scope": "<allowed files or behavior>",
          "priority": 1,
          "depends": [],
          "type": "coding",
          "role_pair": "coding-pair"
        }]
     c. Run: {{binaryName}} add-tasks --tasks-file <path.json> --agent-id {{.AgentID}} --json (create replacement tasks)
     d. Run: {{binaryName}} supersede-task <old-id> <new-id-1>,<new-id-2> --reason "<reason>" --agent-id {{.AgentID}} --json
   - Missing context/docs → add to task description (update NOW)
   - Needs different approach → update scope/guidance (execute NOW)
   - Spec is wrong → fix spec first (update NOW)
3. Execute changes: update task and reassign, or supersede with new approach
4. If breaking into smaller tasks — create them all in this session
5. After analyzing each hypothesis-exhausted task:
   - If you resolved it (superseded, updated guidance, fixed spec): no further action needed for that task
   - If you CANNOT resolve it now: run {{binaryName}} assess-hypothesis-exhausted to record your assessment
     Run: {{binaryName}} assess-hypothesis-exhausted <task-id> --note "<why it cannot be resolved now>" --agent-id {{.AgentID}} --json
     This transitions unresolved exhausted work to BLOCKED so it cannot be reassigned unchanged, and prevents re-waking until new information arrives (new failures, human notes).
6. All state modifications must be executed before you exit.

Do NOT call {{binaryName}} sprint-checkpoint. You must either supersede the task, update its guidance, or assess it. Do NOT defer.
{{- end -}}
